      {
        "id": 49222,
        "name": "TheSoundOfTrees",
        "username": "TheSoundOfTrees",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/da6949/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-12-10T21:48:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I was thinking that with X=0 or 1, damage would be 0 - meaning he can still attack, and can even do damage with the right tools/styles/outside modifiers, and do \"damage bursts\" after a few turns of building up. Toolbox allows for a total of three cards drawn a round. I fear my suggestion would make him too powerful, he would need low HPs to compensate : Black Fist was a reckless fighter !</p><p>I did not try Fixy with damage = 2, but from what I've seen when he plays with Legacy, it could be too much - and make Charge redundant.</p>",
